        11
      ],
      "devanagari": "सूतमागधसंबाधां श्रीमातीमतुलप्रभाम् |\nउच्चाट्टालध्वजवतीं शतघ्नीशतसंकुलाम्",
      "iast": "sūta māgadha sambādhām śrīmatīm atula prabhām |\nuccāṭṭāla dhvajavatīm śataghnī śata saṅkulām",
      "translation": "She that prosperous city Ayodhya is muchly crammed with many a eulogist and panej~nrist, yet she is highly splendorous with many a bastion, flag and hundreds of batteries of canons, and Dasharatha dwells therein.",
      "notes": [
        "Comment: This <em>śataghnī</em> literally that which can kill a thousand people, and it is said to be a canon and also said to be thorny weapon: shataghnii catuH talaa loha kaNTaka sa~ncitaa | ayaH kaNTaka sa~ncchannaa mahatii shilaa -- elaborate accounts of this <em>śataghni</em>, <em>kśipaṇi</em> are there in <em>yajur āraṇyaka</em> ."
      ],
